WEBVTT

00:45:59.625 --> 00:46:01.684
but it has become
suddenly really relevant.

00:46:01.708 --> 00:46:05.583
Were you raised for autonomy
or were you raised for loyalty?

00:46:06.625 --> 00:46:08.309
Think for a moment, people.

00:46:08.333 --> 00:46:13.309
Were you raised with the primary messages
around relationships that said,

00:46:13.333 --> 00:46:15.643
"You have yourself to rely on.

00:46:15.667 --> 00:46:17.559
In the end, it's all about you.

00:46:17.583 --> 00:46:20.684
Nobody's ever going to help you
as well as you can help yourself."

00:46:20.708 --> 00:46:24.393
Ontologically, in a way,
you are alone in this world.

00:46:24.417 --> 00:46:27.351
And how do you think
that influences the way

00:46:27.375 --> 00:46:29.893
that you organize
your relationships around you,

00:46:29.917 --> 00:46:32.934
your concepts of give and take,
your concept of asking for help